.Dd May 27, 2026
.Dt AUTHORITYCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm authorityctl
.Nd control interface for authorityd
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm status
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm shutdown
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm reload
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends administrative commands to a running
.Xr authorityd 8
instance via its control socket.
.Pp
The
.Fl s
option specifies an alternate socket path (default:
.Pa /var/run/authorityd.sock ) .
This is needed when
.Xr authorityd 8
is configured with a non-default
.Va control_socket
path.
Each invocation connects, sends a single command, prints the
result, and exits.
.Pp
The following commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width "shutdown"
.It Cm status
Query the daemon's status and uptime.
The output includes:
.Bl -tag -width "SERVICED" -compact
.It Sy CONFIG
Configuration file path and service manager binary.
.It Sy INTEGRITY
Active
.Xr mac_capability_capprotect 4
shield flags.
.It Sy CLAIMS
All active resource claims, grouped by type (paths, network, jails,
system gates).
Each claim is annotated with its provenance:
.Ql [policy]
for claims from
.Xr authorityd.conf 5
or
.Ql [service, refcount=N]
for dynamic claims created at runtime.
Each claim is verified against the kernel via
.Dv FI_OP_QUERY ;
claims the kernel no longer holds are marked
.Ql [NOT HELD] .
.It Sy SERVICED
Ready/not-ready status and PID of
.Xr serviced 8 .
.El
.Pp
This command does not require root privileges.
.It Cm shutdown
Request a graceful shutdown of
.Xr authorityd 8 .
The daemon terminates its process subtree, releases all capability
runtime resources, and exits.
Requires root.
.It Cm reload
Reload
.Xr authorityd.conf 5
claims and forward
.Dv SIGHUP
to
.Xr serviced 8 ,
which re-scans capability bundles.
Prints a summary of claim changes.
Requires root.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/authorityd.sock"
.It Pa /var/run/authorityd.sock
Unix domain socket used to communicate with
.Xr authorityd 8 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
Privileged commands return
.Er EX_NOPERM
when executed by a non-root user.
If
.Xr authorityd 8
is not running,
.Nm
exits with
.Er EX_UNAVAILABLE .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac_capability 4 ,
.Xr authorityd 8 ,
.Xr servicectl 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
